# Optimized Frontend Verification Process - Fast Development Mode

## WHEN TO USE THIS RULE:
- When making small code changes during active development
- After fixing simple bugs or typos
- When modifying CSS files
- During iterative UI development
- When the assistant needs to quickly verify changes
- AFTER using the full verification process at least once in a session

## DO NOT USE THIS FOR:
- Initial project setup
- After major refactoring
- When package.json is modified
- After changing configuration files
- First verification of a new session

## PROCESS:

### Step 1: Quick Server Health Check
```javascript
// Check if server is responding (NO LONG TIMEOUTS)
const serverStatus = await mcp_desktop_commander_execute_command('curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:4000');

// If server not responding, try hot reload FIRST
if (serverStatus !== "200") {
  console.log('Server not responding, attempting hot reload...');
  await mcp_desktop_commander_execute_command('touch /path/to/project/pages/_app.tsx');
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1000)); // MAX 1 second wait
  
  // Recheck after hot reload
  const secondCheck = await mcp_desktop_commander_execute_command('curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:4000');
  
  if (secondCheck !== "200") {
    console.log('Hot reload failed, switching to FULL VERIFICATION PROCESS');
    // MUST switch to full verification rule
    return 'FALLBACK_TO_FULL_VERIFICATION';
  }
}
```

### Step 2: Quick Browser Error Detection
```javascript
// Navigate without screenshot unless errors found
await mcp_puppeteer_puppeteer_navigate('http://localhost:4000');

// Quick error check - looking for obvious problems only
const hasErrors = await mcp_puppeteer_puppeteer_evaluate(`
  document.body.innerText.includes('Error') || 
  document.body.innerText.includes('failed') ||
  document.body.innerText.includes('Module not found') ||
  document.querySelector('[data-nextjs-error]') !== null
`);

if (hasErrors) {
  console.log('Errors detected, starting diagnosis...');
  // Go to Step 3: Error Diagnosis
} else {
  console.log('✓ Quick verification PASSED');
  return { status: 'PASSED', mode: 'quick' };
}
```

### Step 3: Error Diagnosis (Only if errors detected)
```javascript
const diagnosis = await mcp_puppeteer_puppeteer_evaluate(`
  (function() {
    const fullText = document.body.innerText;
    const errors = [];
    
    // Check for missing module errors
    if (fullText.includes("Module not found")) {
      const match = fullText.match(/Module not found: Can't resolve '([^']+)'/);
      if (match) {
        errors.push({
          type: 'MISSING_MODULE',
          module: match[1],
          solution: 'npm install'
        });
      }
    }
    
    // Check for syntax errors
    if (fullText.includes("SyntaxError")) {
      const lineMatch = fullText.match(/SyntaxError.*?:(\\d+):(\\d+)/);
      errors.push({
        type: 'SYNTAX_ERROR',
        location: lineMatch ? lineMatch[0] : 'unknown',
        solution: 'prettier'
      });
    }
    
    // Check for undefined errors
    if (fullText.includes("TypeError") && fullText.includes("undefined")) {
      errors.push({
        type: 'UNDEFINED_ERROR',
        solution: 'check_imports'
      });
    }
    
    // Check for import errors
    if (fullText.includes("Cannot find module")) {
      const moduleMatch = fullText.match(/Cannot find module '([^']+)'/);
      if (moduleMatch) {
        errors.push({
          type: 'IMPORT_ERROR',
          module: moduleMatch[1],
          solution: 'check_imports'
        });
      }
    }
    
    return errors;
  })()
`);
```

### Step 4: Auto-Fix Attempts (Based on diagnosis)
```javascript
// Try to fix each diagnosed error
for (const error of diagnosis) {
  switch (error.type) {
    case 'MISSING_MODULE':
      console.log(`Auto-fixing: Installing missing module '${error.module}'`);
      await mcp_desktop_commander_execute_command(
        `cd /path/to/project && npm install ${error.module}`
      );
      break;
      
    case 'SYNTAX_ERROR':
      console.log('Auto-fixing: Running prettier to fix syntax');
      await mcp_desktop_commander_execute_command(
        'cd /path/to/project && npx prettier --write .'
      );
      break;
      
    case 'UNDEFINED_ERROR':
    case 'IMPORT_ERROR':
      console.log('Cannot auto-fix import issues, manual intervention needed');
      break;
  }
}

// Wait briefly for fixes to take effect
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 2000));

// Re-run quick verification
return await quickVerification(); // Go back to Step 1
```

### Step 5: Report Results
```javascript
// If auto-fix worked:
console.log('✓ Quick verification PASSED after auto-fix');
return { 
  status: 'PASSED', 
  mode: 'quick',
  fixes_applied: diagnosis.map(d => d.type)
};

// If auto-fix failed:
console.log('❌ Quick verification FAILED - manual intervention required');
return {
  status: 'FAILED',
  mode: 'quick',
  errors: diagnosis,
  action_required: 'Manual fixes needed'
};
```

## ENFORCEMENT RULES:

1. **MUST use this process for minor changes during active development**
2. **MUST fall back to full verification if server restart is needed**
3. **MUST NOT use this for initial setup or major changes**
4. **MUST attempt hot reload before server restart**
5. **MUST complete in under 10 seconds for success cases**
6. **MUST diagnose specific errors before attempting fixes**
7. **MUST report all fixes attempted**

## FALLBACK CONDITIONS:

Switch to FULL VERIFICATION PROCESS if:
- Server doesn't respond after hot reload
- More than 3 errors detected
- Package.json was modified
- Configuration files changed
- First verification of a session
- Auto-fix attempts fail twice

## SUCCESS CRITERIA:

Quick verification PASSES when:
- Server responds with 200
- No error text detected in browser
- No error overlays visible
- Process completes in under 10 seconds

## EXAMPLE USAGE:

```
// After fixing a typo in a component:
Quick verification starting...
✓ Server responding (200)
✓ No errors detected in browser
✓ Quick verification PASSED

// After removing an import accidentally:
Quick verification starting...
⚠️ Errors detected, starting diagnosis...
Found: UNDEFINED_ERROR in MyComponent.tsx
Auto-fixing: Checking imports...
Cannot auto-fix import issues, manual intervention needed
❌ Quick verification FAILED - manual intervention required
```

## WHEN TO ALERT USER:

- When falling back to full verification
- When auto-fix attempts fail
- When manual intervention is required
- When process takes longer than 10 seconds